+- Node pools: interactive (low latency) vs batch (spot, cheaper).
+
+Operational notes
+- Tune MAX_BATCH to balance latency vs throughput. Use smaller values for interactive workloads.
+- Use the interactive nodePool for requests with priority interactive; route batch jobs to a separate queue that maps to batch node pool.
+- Ensure Prometheus exporter for Redis list lengths is available (redis_exporter or custom exporter) so scaling can use queue length.
+- Monitor GPU utilization and tail latencies. If batch jobs saturate GPUs, consider a separate fleet for batch inference.
+
+Troubleshooting
+- If the aggregator returns empty results, check Redis list keys and permissions.
+- If KEDA doesn't scale, validate Prometheus metrics and ScaledObject logs.
